<title>USA: Marathon drops US posted crude 50 cts/bbl.</title>
<headline>Marathon drops US posted crude 50 cts/bbl.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil Co said it cut the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 50 cents a barrel, effective today.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $20.00 a barrel, and West Texas Sour to $18.65 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $20.00 a barrel, and Oklahoma sweet is $20.00.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859-1620</p>
</text>
